.TH LINEMARK 1 "" "noweb contrib"
.SH NAME
linemark \- insert source-location comments into noweb code chunks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B notangle
\fB\-filter\fP '\fBlinemark\fP
[\fB\-L\fP \fIfmt\fP]
[\fB\-c\fP \fIleader\fP]
[\fB\-e\fP]'
\fIfile\fP ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I linemark
is a
.IR noweb (1)
filter that inserts a comment line, by default
.BR "# %L \(dq%F\(dq" ,
wherever the tangled output jumps to a different place in the noweb
source: after the first line of every code chunk (announcing its
second, so that a chunk spliced into the middle of a line never has
its first line broken), before continuation definitions of the same
chunk, and after every line that uses another chunk.
Tangle
.I without
the
.B \-L
option and indentation is preserved, which makes the filter suitable
for indentation-sensitive languages such as Python, for which
.B notangle \-L
produces broken output.
Comment-only lines are exempt from Python's indentation rules, so the
inserted lines are harmless.
Use
.IR nolinemap (1)
to translate tool messages that point into the tangled files back to
the noweb sources.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-L \fIfmt\fP
Set the marker format.
.B %L
expands to the source line number,
.B %F
to the source file name, and
.B %%
to a percent sign; these are the escapes of
.BR "notangle \-L" ,
except that
.B %N
is not supported, because a marker is always exactly one line.
The default is
.BR "# %L \(dq%F\(dq" .
.TP
.B \-c \fIleader\fP
Use
.I leader
as the comment leader in the default format:
.B \-c //
gives
.BR "// %L \(dq%F\(dq" .
When both options are given,
.B \-L
wins.
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-eager
Place every chunk's marker before its first line, as earlier
versions did, and mark after backslash continuations too.
A chunk spliced into the middle of a line then carries the marker
inside the broken line, and a marker after a continuation severs
it, so this suits only consumers that post-process the tangled text
and repair both themselves (vim-noweb's shadow buffers do); in
exchange they get an exact map, with no lines anchored across a
splice.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
notangle -Rfoo.py -filter linemark foo.nw > foo.py
nolinemap python3 foo.py
.fi
.SH BUGS
The first line of a chunk is anchored by counting from the marker
before its use site, so an error on it is reported at the line using
the chunk rather than at its definition.
The same counting covers any leading lines of a chunk that end in a
backslash: a marker there would sever the continuation, so it is
delayed until a line without one, and messages pointing into the
delayed run come out shifted by the length of the splice detour.
A chunk whose first line opens a multi-line string cannot be
protected the same way; the delayed marker lands inside the string.
The very first line of the tangled file has no marker before it at
all; messages pointing there are not translated.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR nolinemap (1),
.IR notangle (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Daniel Bosk <dbosk@kth.se>
